# === Except: one new script added this project (not part of Florido's original repo) -- a
# directory-level ignore like the one above blocks a plain file negation, so each directory level
# down to the file has to be un-ignored in turn (git's own documented behavior for this case) ===
!/experimental_grow-main/
/experimental_grow-main/*
!/experimental_grow-main/experiments/
/experimental_grow-main/experiments/*
!/experimental_grow-main/experiments/pipeline/
/experimental_grow-main/experiments/pipeline/*
!/experimental_grow-main/experiments/pipeline/run_original_cifartile_margaret.slurm

# === nas-challenge-submission-main build artifacts (Makefile: build/run/score) and downloaded
# benchmark data (the multi-hundred-MB train/valid/test .npy arrays fetched by
# run_demeter_margaret.slurm) -- all regenerable, never worth tracking ===
/nas-challenge-submission-main/package/
/nas-challenge-submission-main/scoring/
/nas-challenge-submission-main/datasets/

# === Except: results a margaret run pushes back (predictions + stats + the run log) are small
# (label arrays / text, not training data) and are meant to be tracked -- re-include them despite
# the blanket *.npy/*.pkl/*.log excludes above ===
!/nas-challenge-submission-main/results/
!/nas-challenge-submission-main/results/**